<title>SINGAPORE: SPH half-year net profit up 9.2 pct.</title>
<headline>SPH half-year net profit up 9.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended Feb 28 1997</p>
<p>(in millions of Singapore dollar unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		     172.38   vs    157.85</p>
<p>    Group shares (cents)	  50.42   vs     46.23</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		12.00   vs     10.00</p>
<p>    Turnover			 455.05   vs    439.95</p>
<p>    Trading profit		 203.57   vs    189.47</p>
<p>    Investment income	     34.70   vs     29.73</p>
<p>    Associates (loss)	    (4.04)   vs     (3.69)</p>
<p>Pretax profit		  234.22   vs    215.51</p>
<p>    Tax				 62.07   vs     57.21</p>
<p>    Minorities			 0.23   vs     (0.45)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		  nil    vs     (0.17)</p>
<p>    Dividend pay/register	 May 19/May 5</p>
<p>Note -- Newspaper group Singapore Press Holdings Ltd said advertisment revenue grew 3.4 percent and circulation revenue by one percent. Its results were better than expected as most analysts had predicted flat earnings in the first half.</p>
<p>--Singapoe newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
